.TH SPEECH 1.SH NAMEspeech \- English text into phonemes.SH SYNOPSIS\fBspeech\fR[infile [outfile]].SH DESCRIPTIONThe front half of a speech synthesiser: it translates English into thephonemes that would say it, by the rules for English spelling.  Run bareit prompts\fBEnter english text (Ctrl-Z to end):\fRand prints the transcription of each line typed;\fBhello world\fRcomes out\fBhEHlOW wERld\fR.\fRGiven files it translates the whole of one into the other.  It callsitself\fBPHONEME\fRin its usage line.